    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA rare opportunity to acquire an attractive parcel of land extending to approximately 8.6 acres (3.48 Ha.) in the highly sought-after coastal location of Curragreen, Coast Road, Oranmore. Occupying a prime position between Galway City and Oranmore Village, this unique holding offers a combination of good quality agricultural land, equestrian facilities and direct access to the shoreline.\n\nThe lands are divided into four separate sections, with three paddocks enclosed by a mixture of stone walls and fencing. The lands are of good quality, currently in grass and are well serviced with water troughs located throughout. The property benefits from both water and electricity connections, making it suitable for a range of agricultural, equestrian and recreational uses.\n\nExisting facilities on the property include a number of horse stables, a sand arena requiring upgrading, a storage outbuilding, and a mobile home. Access to the lands is provided from the Coast Road via a laneway leading into the holding. The lands are well laid out and offer excellent potential for agricultural, equestrian or recreational use. A particularly attractive feature is that the holding extends to the shoreline, providing direct access to the sea.\n\nSituated in one of Galway's most sought-after locations between Oranmore and Galway City, the lands enjoy the benefits of a peaceful rural setting while remaining highly accessible to a wide range of services and amenities. Holdings of this size, with established equestrian facilities, good quality land and direct shoreline access, rarely come to the market along the Coast Road.\n\nThis represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a substantial coastal holding with good quality lands, established equestrian facilities and direct access to the shoreline, all within minutes of Oranmore and Galway City."
      },
